CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Negative control for `symbolic_malloc_pointer_identity_index_read`: the
write to `tids[0]` happens-before the reader thread is even created, so
there is no race. Must stay SUCCESSFUL before and after the fix -- confirms
recognising `ID_index` under the if-chain does not turn correctly-ordered
accesses into false alarms.
